@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il36-nouns`
IMPORT `il36-builders`
IMPORT `il36-s1-definitions`
IMPORT `il36-s4-departure`
IMPORT `il36-s5-s6-commencement`
IMPORT `il36-s2-exemption`
IMPORT `il36-s3-entity`
IMPORT `il36-answers`

-- Tests of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law, 5786-2026.
-- Every expected value below was worked by hand from the text of the Law (the transcription's lines are
-- cited in the headings) BEFORE the module was run.  A failing assertion is a finding, never an edit.
-- A day is written YMD year month day.  Money is new shekels.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Fixtures: the persons`

-- Became a resident for the first time on 10 November 2025: a resident for the whole of 2026.
`Pf` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10)
-- Became a resident on 1 July 2026: 184 days of 2026 (31+31+30+31+30+31), six calendar months.
`Pj` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 7 1)
-- Became a resident on 1 March 2026 and elected an adaptation year from the same day (ITO s 14(b)(1)),
-- which runs to 28 February 2027.
`Pm` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and elected an adaptation year from` (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- Ceased to be a resident on 1 July 2027: a resident through 30 June 2027.
`Pc` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `and ceased to be one on` (YMD 2027 7 1)
-- Ceased on 1 July 2026: 181 days of 2026 (31+28+31+30+31+30), six calendar months.
`Pc26` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `and ceased to be one on` (YMD 2026 7 1)
-- Veteran returning resident, became a resident on 5 November 2025.
`Pv` MEANS `a veteran returning resident who became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 5)

§§ `Fixtures: the readings`

`F2` MEANS `fork F2, the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
`F3` MEANS `fork F3, the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
`F4` MEANS `fork F4, the adaptation year`
`F5` MEANS `fork F5, the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
`F6` MEANS `fork F6, the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
`F7` MEANS `fork F7, the residence of the individual in section 3`
`F8` MEANS `fork F8, section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
`F9` MEANS `fork F9, the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`

-- Every switch declined: the model's default.
`R0` MEANS `the readings this model takes where the text does not decide`

GIVEN `the fork` IS A `A fork`
      `the readings` IS A `The readings`
GIVETH A `The readings`
`first reading of` `the fork` `on` `the readings` MEANS `the readings with` `the fork` `set to its first reading` TRUE `in` `the readings`

GIVEN `the fork` IS A `A fork`
      `the readings` IS A `The readings`
GIVETH A `The readings`
`second reading of` `the fork` `on` `the readings` MEANS `the readings with` `the fork` `set to its first reading` FALSE `in` `the readings`

-- Every switch at its first named reading, and at its second.
`R-all-first` MEANS
    `first reading of` `F2` `on` (`first reading of` `F3` `on` (`first reading of` `F4` `on` (`first reading of` `F5` `on` (`first reading of` `F6` `on` (`first reading of` `F7` `on` (`first reading of` `F8` `on` (`first reading of` `F9` `on` `R0`)))))))
`R-all-second` MEANS
    `second reading of` `F2` `on` (`second reading of` `F3` `on` (`second reading of` `F4` `on` (`second reading of` `F5` `on` (`second reading of` `F6` `on` (`second reading of` `F7` `on` (`second reading of` `F8` `on` (`second reading of` `F9` `on` `R0`)))))))

-- One switch set, the rest declined.
`R2-first`  MEANS `first reading of` `F2` `on` `R0`
`R2-second` MEANS `second reading of` `F2` `on` `R0`
`R3-first`  MEANS `first reading of` `F3` `on` `R0`
`R3-second` MEANS `second reading of` `F3` `on` `R0`
`R4-first`  MEANS `first reading of` `F4` `on` `R0`
`R4-second` MEANS `second reading of` `F4` `on` `R0`
`R5-days`   MEANS `first reading of` `F5` `on` `R0`
`R5-months` MEANS `second reading of` `F5` `on` `R0`
`R7-first`  MEANS `first reading of` `F7` `on` `R0`
`R7-second` MEANS `second reading of` `F7` `on` `R0`
`R8-first`  MEANS `first reading of` `F8` `on` `R0`
`R8-second` MEANS `second reading of` `F8` `on` `R0`
`R9-first`  MEANS `first reading of` `F9` `on` `R0`
`R9-second` MEANS `second reading of` `F9` `on` `R0`
-- Two switches set.
`R5-days-6-first`  MEANS `first reading of` `F6` `on` `R5-days`
`R5-days-6-second` MEANS `second reading of` `F6` `on` `R5-days`
`R8-first-9-declined` MEANS `R8-first`
`R4-first-5-days` MEANS `first reading of` `F5` `on` `R4-first`
`R4-second-5-days` MEANS `first reading of` `F5` `on` `R4-second`
`R4-first-5-months` MEANS `second reading of` `F5` `on` `R4-first`
`R4-second-5-months` MEANS `second reading of` `F5` `on` `R4-second`

§§ `Fixtures: shorthand for the questions`

GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings`
      `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`exempt` `the readings` `the person` `the items` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the exempt amount of the person's qualifying income, reading` `the readings` `:` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`

GIVEN `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`exempt by default` `the person` `the items` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the exempt amount of the person's qualifying income` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`

GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings`
      `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
      `the entity`   IS AN `An entity`
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of an entity's business income`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`entity exempt` `the readings` `the person` `the entity` `the items` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the exempt business income of the entity, reading` `the readings` `:` `the person` `entity` `the entity` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`

§§ `Section 1 — "עולה", "תושב חוזר ותיק", "קרוב" (transcription lines 11, 13, 15)`

-- An oleh visa or certificate; or a class entitled to an absorption basket; but not a person whose
-- citizenship was cancelled under s 11 of the Citizenship Law.
#ASSERT `s 1 — an immigrant` `Pf`
#ASSERT `s 1 — an immigrant` (`an immigrant counted in an absorption basket class, who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — an immigrant` (`an oleh whose Israeli citizenship was cancelled under section 11 of the Citizenship Law, who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — an immigrant` `Pv`
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — an immigrant` (`a person who is neither an immigrant nor a veteran returning resident and became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 1 1))

-- Section 14(a)'s veteran returning resident, and a certificate of the Ministry of Aliyah and Integration.
#ASSERT `s 1 — a veteran returning resident` `Pv`
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — a veteran returning resident` (`a returning resident with no certificate, who became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — a veteran returning resident` `Pf`

-- A relative as the Ordinance defines it, but not a company wholly owned by the immigrant.
#ASSERT `s 1 — an item received from a relative` (`an employment income received from a relative of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — an item received from a relative` (`an employment income received from a company wholly owned by the immigrant, of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — an item received from a relative` (`an employment income of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))

§§ `Section 1 — "הכנסה מזכה" by its kind (transcription line 10)`

`Q-first`  MEANS `income attributed under section 62A is qualifying income although it comes from a transparent corporation`
`Q-second` MEANS `income attributed under section 62A is not qualifying income because it comes from a transparent corporation`

#ASSERT `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `Q-first` `:` (`an employment income of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `Q-first` `:` (`a business income of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- Rent, interest and the like are not income under section 2(1) or (2).
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `Q-first` `:` (`an income from another source (such as rent or interest) of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- "שאינה הכנסה אחרת"
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `Q-first` `:` (`a business income that is other income under section 62A(d), of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- "הכנסה חייבת"
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `Q-first` `:` (`an employment income that is not chargeable income, of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- "הכנסה מיגיעה אישית"
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `Q-first` `:` (`a business income that is not income from personal exertion, of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- Attributed from a transparent corporation, not under section 62A: out under both readings.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `Q-first` `:` (`a business income attributed from a transparent corporation, of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `Q-second` `:` (`a business income attributed from a transparent corporation, of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- Attributed from a transparent corporation under section 62A: fork F2.
#ASSERT `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `Q-first` `:` (`a business income attributed from a transparent corporation under section 62A, of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `Q-second` `:` (`a business income attributed from a transparent corporation under section 62A, of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- The declined reading is never handed to this rule.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — qualifying income by its kind, reading the exception for section 62A as` `a case that turns on the exception for income attributed under section 62A is declined` `:` (`a business income attributed from a transparent corporation under section 62A, of` 100 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))

